      "content": "To differentiate between oxidized and reduced firing atmospheres, inspect the fragments for discoloration patterns and areas of oxidation. Oxidized firing often produces more pronounced turquoise, turquoise-gray, or bluish coloration, especially in areas of high iron concentration. Conversely, reduced firing tends to produce more orange or rust-colored hues. Additionally, check for salt-and-pepper patterns, which can indicate uneven oxidation.",
