    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, I think you might have that backwards. Usually, oxidized firing results in reds and yellows because of the iron, and reduced firing is what gives you the dark/black/gray colors, right? Also, does the specific texture or porosity of the shard change depending on the atmosphere? I'm seeing some very irregular, almost pitted surfaces on these specific fragments.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
